From 917f6fd490861f8da9c7ea8556cf70f8214fcb42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban operator: be/being govern only across
 adverbs; any spaced or verb-glued hyphen run is a dash; one replica caller
 check per call

PR #2037 review nits (review 5889053807, card t_01a1d44a80b28f8c):

1. be/being were in _NOT_CLAIM, so they governed from anywhere in the 3-word
   window: "To be safe I posted the summary to t_X" and "Being thorough I
   posted to t_X" stopped being claims (an undocumented fail-open). be/being
   now govern only when nothing but adverbs stands between them and the verb
   ("to be posted", "to be soon posted", "is being quickly sent"); those two
   read as claims again. "Queued to be posted", "Queued: to be posted" and
   "Queued (to be posted" stay non-claims.
2. A hyphen run of any length that touches a space or the clause edge on
   either side is a dash boundary: "Not done --- posted", "Not done -posted"
   and "Not done- posted" are claims. Intra-word hyphens ("re-posted") are
   unaffected.
3. apply_incoming runs _caller_replica_refusal once per call and passes it to
   _home_check and _caller_refusal, instead of repeating the task_runs and
   claimed-event replica queries. Replica refusal still runs before the
   deferral.
4. _home_check's docstring states the bounded cost of a deferral: each tick
   pages the request tail past a held watermark, and a caller that passes the
   replica checks but fails Board evidence can hold the watermark up to
   CREATION_SYNC_GRACE_S.

Proof: RED at 26a1896f38 (7 new cases fail: 6 classifier, 1 replica-once).
GREEN: 9 operator/consent files, 270 passed. Mutants 11/11 killed.
